/* Standard evolution goals.

   Goal is an authoring-time file grouping only. `choose:` supplies candidate
   function calls; it does not select or execute a candidate.

   The `path(...)` guard and the `path_delta(...)` argument both read
   data/paths.tsv (P52). Neither this file nor recipes.chg names a source
   concept: adding GO, WANT, COME or any other source to a target is one new
   data row. A verb whose core sense is not a listed source for the target
   simply yields no candidate, which is a legitimate result (P70). */

package std:grammaticalization:
    schema = conlang.functions/v1

function Future(target [Verb]):
    choose:
        VerbToTense(target, tense: FUTURE, result_category: Aux, delta: path_delta(target, core, FUTURE)) / path(target, core, FUTURE)

/* A FINISH verb may supply a perfect function and become a bound marker.
   Goal evaluation only yields the candidate; selection remains explicit. */
function Perfect(target [Verb]):
    choose:
        VerbToTense(target, tense: PERFECT, result_category: Bound, delta: path_delta(target, core, PERFECT)) / path(target, core, PERFECT)
